## Installing the Chart

To install the chart with the release name `my-release`:

```
helm repo add perses https://perses.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update
helm install my-release perses/perses
```

Please also refer to the [Perses installation documentation](https://perses.dev/helm-charts/docs/installation/) for additional configuration options and usage guidelines when using the Perses Helm chart.

## Handling Sensitive Data

The Helm chart supports security and authentication settings that may contain sensitive data, including encryption keys and OIDC credentials. Do not commit secrets to Git or store them directly in plain-text Helm values files. Instead, provide sensitive values through Kubernetes Secrets or another secure mechanism.

### OIDC Provider Credentials

For instructions on configuring OIDC provider credentials with a Kubernetes Secret, see the [OIDC provider guide](https://perses.dev/helm-charts/docs/auth-secrets/).

## Uninstalling the Chart

To uninstall/delete the my-release deployment:

```
helm delete my-release
```

## Upgrading

For upgrade instructions, including handling breaking changes between versions, see the [Upgrade Guide](../../docs/upgrade-guide.md).
